lenses.coverage:
I wrote my own recount script (work/find-recount/recount.py). It does not import addendum8_tables.py or the analysis functions of confirm.py or replicate.py. It regenerates FRESH-4 with fresh4.make() (digest 6159d55f97e57301; names, kinds, stages and modulo flags identical to the stored ones; 800 unique names) and recomputes from the stored rows:
- every evaluation-table cell (sound/verified, held-out B, FRESH-4 and its 756 list tasks; the union counts 39/125/116);
- all 46 'Comparisons' lines, including the two FRESH-3 lines from replication.json;
- primary (exact p 5.82e-9), new vs old, old vs any, other outputs;
- kinds (a)/(b)/(c) and budget-bound;
- the five endings and their grades;
- both strata tables (10 strata x 2);
- 'more than re-pairing';
- by-routine (27 routines);
- leave-one-routine-out (all 35);
- the routine-removal procedure;
- both cluster tests;
- the FRESH-2-mix standardisation;
- whole-pool soundness, re-evaluated with my own code;
- new-only by symbol;
- R1 chain, R2 detail, R3 on FRESH-4; R3 on held-out B;
- the three ablations; the R1 step-2 gains/losses (14/9);
- D1-D14 against the registered wording and its conditional rules (D2 only if D1 passes; D10 not scored when not testable): 9 hits, 4 misses, 1 not scored confirmed;
- per-row counts, sound counts, spent, and records-solved = programs.

In stored mode 236 comparison items (most of them multi-number dicts) matched and 5 did not. All 5 come from the dream bool/int issue.

I also checked the loop table from the timeline: unsolved 93/49/37, teacher shares 230,107/436,734/578,378, taught 27/14/5, trials 21/10/6, accepted 15/4/0, learn 121/165/177/177, held-out B verified 27/45/50. Also the training ceiling 189,239,903 (sum of budget x tasks), spent 103,919,484, and C2old/C2new/C1new arithmetic. The recursive symbols' folded programs are text-equal to cycle-2 discoveries (s22: 1, s23: 7 of 11, s24: 1, s25: 1).

Strata membership was rebuilt from data:
- routine names parsed from the task names agree with the stages;
- the divisibility family: Addendum 7 lists 7 names, while fresh3.MODULO adds evens and odds, which do not occur in FRESH-4, so the two agree in effect (236 tasks with a divisibility routine, 39 with slice-k-n);
- provenance via fresh4.provenance: 336/400/64/141, first stage 673;
- dream pairs (676) and the 220 pair-dreamt tasks match. Exact dream reproduction does not (42 against 45; finding 2). 35 more tasks match a dreamt pair only in reverse order; the registration does not say whether order counts, so I did not report it.

Soundness with my own verdicts covered all 406 distinct (task, program) pairs in the FRESH-4 rows:
- the stored method replicated with strict element types;
- 400 own in-range draws;
- 404 wide draws at a 2,000,000-step budget;
- 3,000 in-range draws plus non-negative-long and negative splits for the 196 programs on the discordant tasks of R3, the primary and new against old.

Under (i), 0 stored-sound verdicts flip and 1 stored-not-sound flips (the step-budget case). Under (ii), 74 stored-sound flip and the same 1 not-sound flips. Every agreeing program had 200 inputs of evidence; thin evidence is empty.

What did not break:
- strict bool-vs-int element checks change no sound verdict;
- program and record keys all carry a partition prefix; programs and rejected are disjoint; sound is a subset of programs; the same program has the same verdict in every row;
- no kinds inconsistency (no 'no public match' task has matched=True);
- no gen0 rung matched where the top rung did not;
- all 16 registered sha256 hashes match the copy;
- in range, R3 has no doubtful task among its 107 discordant ones.

Not recomputed: held-out B soundness (audit_all) and the held-out B R1 sound trajectory; the soundness of the teachers' discoveries on learning tasks. For those I used the stored verdicts.
